# One block per VM, in ~/.ssh/config on the Mac. Your ~/.ssh/config is never versioned.
#
# For an Azure ML compute instance, do not write a block by hand. Run `azml-ssh-host add <instance>` instead
# (docs/azml-compute.md). It reads the instance from Azure and writes its own block at the top of the file.
#
# The alias on the Host line is the WT_HOST value that install.sh records when it runs on that VM.
# `wt -H <vm> …`, the task picker (⌃⌥⌘T) and VS Code Remote-SSH all use this name too.
# If you can, keep it short, lowercase and free of dots: it ends up on the row's second line as @<vm>.

Host vm-a
    HostName 203.0.113.10        # the VM's public IP or DNS name
    Port 22                      # the default; some hosts listen elsewhere, and a compute instance always does
    User ubuntu                  # the account you created on the VM
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
    IdentitiesOnly yes           # use only this key, not every key in the agent
    ServerAliveInterval 30       # keepalive, so a sleeping laptop does not silently drop the session
    ServerAliveCountMax 6        # give up after ~3 minutes; cmux usually reconnects after a brief dropout
                                 # after a Wi-Fi network switch, recover a suspended task row with wt attach
    AddKeysToAgent yes           # add the key to the agent on first use, so a passphrase is asked once
    UseKeychain yes              # macOS only; remove on Linux
